            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of coronary artery disease in hemodialysis patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery disease is important in patients with hemodialysis because it relates with prognosis. Characteristics of coronary lesions are severe calcification, diffuse disease and multi-vessel disease. Coronary artery bypass is effective to improve long-term prognosis; however, non-cardiac complication rate is high. Percutaneous coronary intervention is also effective but rotablator is required for severe calcified arteries. Complete revascularization can improve long-term prognosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
